description 58 is identified by "http://example.org/analysis/description/58".

description 58 has the type "iopa:BindingRequirement".

description 58 is a legal rule.

description 58 has the label "Article 79".

description 58 has for "iopa:affects" the resource interop 13.

description 58 has for "cav:valueDescription" the value "1. ENISA shall organise activities to promote the uptake of adopted European cybersecurity certification schemes, including by maintaining the website referred to in paragraph 2 of this Article. 2. ENISA shall maintain and regularly update a dedicated website providing public information on the following: (a)European cybersecurity certification schemes; (b)the fees associated with the maintenance of each European cybersecurity certification scheme; (c) relevant ENISA technical specifications; (d)European cybersecurity certificates and EU statements of conformity, including information with regard to such certificates and statements which are no longer valid, or which are suspended, withdrawn or expired; (e)relevant supplementary cybersecurity information provided in accordance with Article 84(2); (f)summaries of peer reviews pursuant to Article 89(7); (g)technical specifications referenced in a European cybersecurity certification scheme pursuant to Article 74(10). 3.Where applicable, thewebsite referred to in paragraph 2 shall also indicatethe national cybersecurity certification schemes that have been replaced by a European cybersecurity certification scheme.".

description 58 is established in "https://data.europa.eu/eli/dl/proc/2026/11/cod/doc/com/COM_2026_11/FINAL/eng/art_79".

description 58 has the digital dimension data.

description 58 has the digital dimension data flow.

description 58 involves the process maintaining information website mandates enisa to collect process maintain.

description 58 produces item 58 action.

description 58 references data with relevance to the european individual cybersecurity skills.

description 58 has the description "1. ENISA shall organise activities to promote the uptake of adopted European cybersecurity certification schemes, including by maintaining the website referred to in paragraph 2 of this Article. 2. ENISA shall maintain and regularly update a dedicated website providing public information on the following: (a)European cybersecurity certification schemes; (b)the fees associated with the maintenance of each European cybersecurity certification scheme; (c) relevant ENISA technical specifications; (d)European cybersecurity certificates and EU statements of conformity, including information with regard to such certificates and statements which are no longer valid, or which are suspended, withdrawn or expired; (e)relevant supplementary cybersecurity information provided in accordance with Article 84(2); (f)summaries of peer reviews pursuant to Article 89(7); (g)technical specifications referenced in a European cybersecurity certification scheme pursuant to Article 74(10). 3.Where applicable, thewebsite referred to in paragraph 2 shall also indicatethe national cybersecurity certification schemes that have been replaced by a European cybersecurity certification scheme.".


